  why: the erase and the write replace what the board runs, and esptool then restarts the chip with its watchdog where it has one, because a plain reset can leave an ESP32-S3 in download mode
  running: <python> -m esptool --chip esp32s3 --port /dev/cu.usbmodem101 erase-flash
